    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Allport sits on flat, low‑lying Delta land, making it prone to tornadoes and ice storms.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/allport_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Allport experiences a humid subtropical climate with hot, humid summers and mild winters typical of the Arkansas Delta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/allport_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Allport began in the 1870s as an African‑American settlement where freed slaves bought small plots on flood‑prone alluvial soils along Crooked Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/allport_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Allport’s early farms were part of the cotton‑producing Arkansas Delta, giving freed Black residents modest farming opportunities.",
